  "result": "Fixed. All 8 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/pricing.py:10`, `line_subtotal` checked `line.qty > BULK_THRESHOLD`. With the threshold at 10, that only gave the discount at 11 or more, so buying exactly 10 got nothing. I changed it to `>=`. This is the only place the discount is calculated: the order totals and tax both come from `line_subtotal`, so they're fixed too.\n\n**Tests:** the existing `test_bulk_discount` already covered exactly 10 units and was failing before the fix (it got 1083 instead of the expected 1028). I also added two tests:\n- 9 units gets no discount (total 974), so the threshold isn't now too low.\n- 4 units plus 6 more of the same item in one cart reach 10 together and get the discount.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
